Drop Ink's toolchains_llvm usage so Ink can be used as a dependency.

toolchains_llvm's `llvm` module extension fails outright for any module that
is not the root:

    Error in fail: Only the root module can use the 'llvm' extension

Ink configures it to get a host C++ toolchain, which works when Ink is the
root module but makes Ink undepend-able from anywhere else. Crubit pulls in
toolchains_llvm too, so both ends of this build hit it.

We register the host toolchain from //MODULE.bazel instead (apple_cc on macOS),
so nothing here is lost.

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -48,15 +48,10 @@
 go_sdk = use_extension("@rules_go//go:extensions.bzl", "go_sdk")
 go_sdk.download(version = "1.23.6")
 
-# Configure and register the LLVM toolchain for host builds by default:
-bazel_dep(name = "toolchains_llvm", version = "1.5.0")
+# The host C++ toolchain is registered by the root module. toolchains_llvm
+# refuses to run its `llvm` extension for anything but the root module, so a
+# module that configures it cannot be depended on.
 
-llvm = use_extension("@toolchains_llvm//toolchain/extensions:llvm.bzl", "llvm")
-llvm.toolchain(llvm_version = "19.1.0")
-use_repo(llvm, "llvm_toolchain")
-
-register_toolchains("@llvm_toolchain//:all")
-
 # Configure the Android NDK toolchain for NDK builds. Don't register that here so it's not required
 # for builds that don't need it. Those configs can register those in --extra_toolchains.
 bazel_dep(name = "rules_android_ndk", version = "0.1.3")
